WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.700
Mario jumped onto the video game scene over&nbsp;
forty years ago, but there is so much more to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.080
learn about everyone's favorite plumber before you&nbsp;
head to the theaters for his next big adventure.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.120
Everyone knows who Mario is, and that's&nbsp;
no accident. Nintendo has meticulously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.320
created one of gaming's biggest franchises&nbsp;
going all the way back to their flagship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.180
character's debut appearance in 1981's&nbsp;
"Donkey Kong" arcade game. This series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.620
has a long and proud history as one of&nbsp;
the most consistent, entertaining, fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.420
and fresh franchises in all of gaming that&nbsp;
constantly pushes the boundaries of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.220
genre. That's exactly why this newest film&nbsp;
adaptation is so highly anticipated by fans.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.500
Beginning with 1983's "Mario Bros" arcade&nbsp;
game, Nintendo transitioned the franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.240
into home entertainment systems in 1985&nbsp;
with the release of "Super Mario Bros"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.980
on the NES. Players enjoyed controlling&nbsp;
both Mario and Luigi as they traversed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.480
the Mushroom Kingdom in search of Princess&nbsp;
Peach. This core game loop continued into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.800
later installments on home consoles and&nbsp;
handhelds before making the leap to 3D.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:07.140
"It'sa me! Mario! Hello!"

00:01:08.628 --> 00:01:13.140
As gaming technology advanced, so too did&nbsp;
the complexity of games being released on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.900
each successive console. With the release&nbsp;
of 1996's "Super Mario 64," new features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.340
continued to be added to make each Mario&nbsp;
adventure more interesting. The franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.120
remains an essential piece of gaming&nbsp;
history. Only time will tell which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.480
aspects of this prestige franchise&nbsp;
will show up in the upcoming movie.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.520
Originally, Mario was supposed to jump&nbsp;
into the big screen on December 21,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.860
2022. Sadly for fans hoping to spend&nbsp;
the holiday season with Luigi, Bowser,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.420
and Princess Peach, that release date&nbsp;
was pushed back to 2023. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.320
we won't have to wait much longer to see&nbsp;
Mario's adventures in the Mushroom Kingdom.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.860
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" has&nbsp;
a new release date of April 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.960
2023. We're expecting the movie to make quite&nbsp;
a bit of cash during its box office run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.460
as it won't have any animated competition&nbsp;
trying to draw similar crowds. As for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:07.440
Nintendo's homeland of Japan, the film will&nbsp;
open on April 28, just a few weeks later.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.120
Universal and Illumination spared no&nbsp;
expense when it comes to casting "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.320
Super Mario Bros. Movie." Voicing Mario&nbsp;
is none other than Star-Lord himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.120
Chris Pratt. Charlie Day of "It's Always Sunny&nbsp;
in Philadelphia" joins him as Mario's brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.460
Luigi. Anya Taylor-Joy of "The Queen's Gambit"&nbsp;
and "The Menu" plays Princess Peach. We can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.080
also expect to hear the scarier-than-usual&nbsp;
tones of Jack Black as antagonist Bowser.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:36.120
In supporting roles, Keegan-Michael Key portrays&nbsp;
Toad, Seth Rogen steps in as Donkey Kong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:41.220
and Fred Armisen is the voice of Cranky Kong. The&nbsp;
announcement also notes that Charles Martinet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.560
who's voiced Mario and other notable characters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.860
the video games since the '90s,&nbsp;
will have "surprise cameos."

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.600
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" is the result&nbsp;
of two powerful forces coming together:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.400
Nintendo and Illumination. And that&nbsp;
collaborative dynamic is represented in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.840
the film's producers. On one side, you've&nbsp;
got Chris Meledandri, the producer behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.760
the "Despicable Me" and "Sing" franchises. On&nbsp;
the other side, you've got Shigeru Miyamoto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.720
the genius who created Mario as well&nbsp;
as characters like Donkey Kong, Link,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.980
and Zelda. Together, they bring their animation&nbsp;
and video game knowledge to the big screen.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.020
As for who's directing, "The Super Mario Bros.&nbsp;
Movie" recruited two figures who are quite adept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:24.660
at handling animated projects. Aaron Horvath and&nbsp;
Michael Jelenic the filmmakers behind "Teen Titans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:29.400
Go! To the Movies" helm the picture. They're&nbsp;
working from a script penned by Matthew Fogel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:34.500
who previously wrote "The LEGO Movie 2: The&nbsp;
Second Part" and "Minions: The Rise of Gru."

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.480
As you might expect, "The Super Mario Bros.&nbsp;
Movie" got the standard rating for family fare:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:44.580
PG. It perfectly lines up with Illumination's&nbsp;
other offerings like "Despicable Me" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.080
"The Secret Life of Pets." According to the&nbsp;
Classification and Ratings Administration's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.280
website, the movie has earned its PG&nbsp;
rating for "action and mild violence."

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.840
We expect the violence to be incredibly&nbsp;
mild. Anyone familiar with the games knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.640
Mario's propensity for dishing out pain only&nbsp;
extends to jumping on Goombas or occasionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.300
throwing fireballs at a Koopa Troopas.&nbsp;
Even the trailers show that the action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.380
will be light-hearted and comical, as&nbsp;
depicted when Donkey Kong hilariously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:14.040
slaps our favorite plumber around or&nbsp;
when a penguin army assaults Bowser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:18.360
with snowballs and the Koopa Kamek returns&nbsp;
the favor by magically tossing them aside.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.020
Mario is one of the most popular&nbsp;
video game characters in history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:25.980
and the "Super Mario Bros" franchise&nbsp;
has always been a fundamental part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:30.300
gaming culture as a result. Because of this&nbsp;
popularity, it should come as no surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.620
that this isn't the first time Mario has&nbsp;
graced the silver screen since his debut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:40.380
appearance in 1981. Nintendo has tried multiple&nbsp;
times to turn Mario into a multimedia character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.880
beyond just video games, but they've never&nbsp;
been particularly successful in the past.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.300
The first time Mario and friends&nbsp;
ever appeared in a feature film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.560
was in a 1986 animated adventure&nbsp;
picture named "Super Mario Bros.:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.420
The Great Mission to Rescue Princess Peach!"&nbsp;
Since Mario had already achieved significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:01.740
popularity in his home country of Japan,&nbsp;
producers saw an opportunity to make a cheap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:07.560
60-minute anime based around Mario and Luigi's&nbsp;
usual goal of rescuing Princess Peach from Bowser.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.300
Another more infamous big screen adaptation&nbsp;
was in the 1993 live-action film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:18.180
"Super Mario Bros," starring Bob Hoskins&nbsp;
as Mario and John Leguizamo as Luigi. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:24.060
movie was a total flop, currently holding&nbsp;
an abysmal 29% rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:32.040
"See ya' later, alligator."

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:36.780
The people who made "The Super Mario Bros.&nbsp;
Movie" certainly know their Mario history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.700
as the film is filled with all sorts of Easter&nbsp;
eggs and throwbacks for fans. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.300
both the film's official trailer and&nbsp;
a character poster show our heroes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:50.040
driving down the Rainbow Road, a thoroughfare&nbsp;
instantly recognizable to "Mario Kart" fans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:54.840
Peach can even be seen riding a motorcycle,&nbsp;
paying homage to her outfit design that goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.640
all the way back to "Mario Kart Wii." Expect&nbsp;
homages to plenty of other worlds as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.640
from "Luigi's Mansion" to the&nbsp;
original "Super Mario Bros."

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:07.200
On top of that, it looks like our titular&nbsp;
plumber dons quite a few super suits throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.640
his adventure. In a teaser for the film, we&nbsp;
witness Mario's showdown with Donkey Kong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:17.640
where he puts on a literal catsuit, turning him&nbsp;
into Cat Mario from "Super Mario 3D World." In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.560
the trailer, we also see him soaring around in the&nbsp;
Tanooki Suit, which hails from "Super Mario Bros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.660
3." We also know that quite a few classic Mario&nbsp;
baddies appear in the movie, from the Hammer Bros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:33.660
and the sorcerer Kamek to Goombas, Bob-ombs,&nbsp;
Piranha Plants, Buzzy Beetles, and Shy Guys.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:38.940
We also suspect that elements from Mario's big&nbsp;
space-bound adventures might come into play. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:44.100
shots of upcoming Mario-themed McDonald's toys&nbsp;
revealed a Luma, an adorable star-like creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.960
from "Super Mario Galaxy." Of course, there are&nbsp;
even references to unique "Mario" properties in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.460
the marketing. During the Super Bowl, fans&nbsp;
were treated to a "Mario Bros." promo that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:57.780
acted as a commercial for Mario and Luigi's&nbsp;
plumbing service. In the mock advertisement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:02.460
we're treated to the same Mario rap that's also&nbsp;
the incredibly cheesy theme of "The Super Mario&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.080
Bros. Super Show!," a series that would open&nbsp;
each episode with that plumbing hip-hop beat.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.460
Mario as a character has completely&nbsp;
transcended the video game franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:16.320
that created him by becoming a true, bona&nbsp;
fide pop culture icon. Everyone's favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:21.060
plumber is a universally recognized symbol&nbsp;
of Nintendo and gaming in general thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:24.480
his unique place as both a leading&nbsp;
character and a corporate mascot.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.160
Mario is an essential part of Nintendo's&nbsp;
business strategy since the "Super Mario"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:34.080
games make millions of dollars with each release,&nbsp;
but this character also has staying power with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:38.820
everyone. According to Guinness World Records,&nbsp;
Mario is one of the biggest and most instantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:44.220
recognized video game characters ever made by a&nbsp;
huge margin. He was officially named the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:50.160
"Most Recognizable Video Game Character" in&nbsp;
2009, only getting beat out by Pac-Man by 1%.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:55.380
According to a statement by Mario's creator,&nbsp;
Shigeru Miyamoto, during an official briefing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.380 --> 00:08:00.840
his iconic character even has notable comparisons&nbsp;
to Disney's Mickey Mouse. Miyamoto said,

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.560
"I felt bad that Mickey Mouse, who&nbsp;
had been hugely popular among fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.940
including myself, for 60 years at that&nbsp;
point, was even being compared to Mario,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.340
who had just been around&nbsp;
for a few years back then."

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:14.160
As anyone with an internet&nbsp;
connection can tell you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.720
it can get pretty heated online when fans&nbsp;
discuss their obsessions over social media.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.320
While you might think that the fanbase&nbsp;
for Nintendo's flagship franchise would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.640
be on the friendlier side since the source&nbsp;
material is so colorful, you'd be surprised.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.360
With the release of "The Super Mario&nbsp;
Bros." trailer, fans have gone on record&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:35.460
to voice their opinions both positive and&nbsp;
negative about the new footage. While the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:39.060
consensus seems to lean towards fans&nbsp;
loving the character designs, humor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:43.560
and storytelling of the trailer they also&nbsp;
generally are unsold on Nintendo's choice of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:48.420
leading man. As mentioned, Mario is voiced by&nbsp;
Chris Pratt who seems to be using his regular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:53.160
voice to play the character, rather than&nbsp;
imitating Mario's iconic Italian accent.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:57.360
This was noted by many fans on Twitter&nbsp;
who commented that the supporting cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:02.760
featuring Charlie Day, Ana Taylor-Joy, and Jack&nbsp;
Black will do the heavy lifting for this film.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:03.780
"No pressure."

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:08.760
We're entering a golden age of video game&nbsp;
adaptations with slam dunks like "Sonic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:13.320
the Hedgehog" and HBO's "The Last of Us"&nbsp;
proving that the curse of bad movies based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.460
on games can be broken. That being said,&nbsp;
there's a reason people thought that curse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:21.480
existed in the first place since so many&nbsp;
terrible adaptations have been made over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:25.680
the years. "The Super Mario Bros Movie"&nbsp;
has the potential to be the next example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:30.600
of a video game movie done right, but only if&nbsp;
the filmmakers learned from previous mistakes.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.700
Video game movies have a reputation for being&nbsp;
cheap cash-ins of popular gaming franchises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.360
made hastily and with little regard&nbsp;
for their source material. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.180
worst examples of this has to&nbsp;
be the "Resident Evil" films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.860
which forsake everything good about Capcom's&nbsp;
survival horror series by presenting big,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:53.760
over-the-top spectacles and not much more.&nbsp;
2002's "Resident Evil" has only a 35% rating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:58.560
on Rotten Tomatoes, but each successive entry&nbsp;
gets even worse reviews across the board.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.760
"Mortal Kombat" is another arcade-based&nbsp;
franchise that has suffered from lackluster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:07.500
adaptations since the first movie&nbsp;
in 1995, despite enjoying a cult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.220
following these days. With the star&nbsp;
power behind the upcoming Mario movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:15.660
it's unlikely this adaptation will join&nbsp;
the pantheon of bad video game flicks.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:20.520
Like with most major franchise films today,&nbsp;
there's potential for countless spinoffs if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:25.440
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" does well at&nbsp;
the box office. In a 2021 interview with Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:31.020
Company, Nintendo's global president Shuntaro&nbsp;
Furukawa said that the powers-that-be have no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.860
intention of rushing things unless they're&nbsp;
certain there's a market for it. He said,

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:39.300
"Animation, in general, is something that we&nbsp;
are looking into, and not just this franchise."

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:43.080
One of the big movies that could come&nbsp;
down the pipeline if "The Super Mario&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:48.660
Bros. Movie" is successful is a standalone film&nbsp;
dedicated to Donkey Kong, the beloved gorilla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:53.820
character voiced by Seth Rogen in this upcoming&nbsp;
adaptation. According to Giant Freaking Robot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:58.860
the film is already in development at Illumination&nbsp;
but the details on its potential plot remain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.640
thin. It's likely, however, that many of&nbsp;
the characters introduced in "The Super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:07.020
Mario Bros. Movie" will make appearances&nbsp;
in this proposed Donkey Kong solo feature.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.740
Another spinoff we can expect in years&nbsp;
to come is a "Luigi's Mansion" movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.180
based on the series of action-adventure&nbsp;
games. Luigi's voice actor, Charlie Day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:19.260
expressed interest in the project in an&nbsp;
interview with Comicbook.com, saying,

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:23.820
"Yeah, my son was just playing Luigi's&nbsp;
Mansion the other day on his Switch. Look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:29.220
I'm thrilled to get the opportunity, I grew up&nbsp;
playing Super Mario Brothers as did everyone I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:33.600
know so, we'll see! It's like anything&nbsp;
else in life, I'll go if I'm invited!"

